 "response": "Vililux's budget is now **$3372K**. I worked through every record by hand. I did not do a separate second pass to check the arithmetic.\n\n**Method**\n1. **Authority:** Only Finance Office records change the budget. Messages from Sales, Facilities, Engineering, Legal, Marketing, Vendor, Operations and PMO do not count. Finance Office notes that do not change the budget (reminders, audit notes, room changes) are also ignored.\n2. **Starting point:** #0001 sets the budget to $2550K. It is the only \"set to\" record.\n3. **Withdrawal chains:** Each withdrawal is valid only if it has not itself been withdrawn, so I followed every chain to its last link. Examples:\n   - #0002 (+$218K) is withdrawn. #0003 withdraws it, #0051 withdraws #0003, and #1056 withdraws #0051. That restores #0003, so #0002 stays removed.\n   - #0044 (\u2212$299K) stands. The chain from #0059 up to #1532 has eight links, and the last one leaves the withdrawal of #0044 cancelled.\n   - #0006 (+$483K) is withdrawn. The chain runs #0009 \u2192 #0021 \u2192 #0195 \u2192 #0287 \u2192 #0939.\n4. **Total:** All remaining Finance Office increases and decreases, applied once each in record order, add up to a net change of **+$822K**.\n\n**Result:** $2550K + $822K = $3372K.\n\nANSWER: $3372K",
